## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, on-device NLP that yields actionable summaries from multilingual consumer reviews, a realistic Instacart/Amazon use case, without network dependency.

## Key Concepts
- On-device multilang NLP under tight size constraints
- Feature extraction via lightweight POS or rules
- Sentiment aggregation and justification
- Privacy-first data labeling and offline evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreFeature(feature, sentences) {
  let score = 0;
  for (const s of sentences) {
    if (s.toLowerCase().includes(feature)) {
      if (/\b(good|great|excellent|loved)\b/.test(s)) score += 1;
      if (/\b(bad|worst|terrible|hate)\b/.test(s)) score -= 1;
    }
  }
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle negation and language switch within a single sentence?
- How would you validate usefulness of summaries to buyers?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical system design for regulatory compliance in multilingual content environments, focusing on per-language calibration, privacy preservation, and safe deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual models with language-specific adapters
- Per-language risk calibration and drift detection mechanisms
- Privacy-preserving logging and active learning frameworks
- Gradual rollout, canary deployments, and automated rollback triggers

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing and scoring
function scoreContent(text) {
  const lang = detectLanguage(text);
  const adapter = getLanguageAdapter(lang);
  const riskScore = adapter.predict(text);
  return { language: lang, riskScore, decision: moderate(riskScore) };
}
```

## Why This Question Matters

